    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0271" n="177" xml:id="pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/1025: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >McCafferty</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-17T12:00:00-05:00">December 17,
                        1930—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>74. Your 105, December 16, 8 p.m. Please report at once what American interests
                    may be affected by the present situation in Guatemala and consequently require
                    protection.</p>
                <p>Has Mr. Edwin C. Wilson arrived?<anchor n="1" xml:id="d132-f1"/> If so, transmit
                    his opinion with regard to the situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
